* {{audio|en|En-au-cop-out.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[avoidance|Avoidance]] or [[inadequate]] [[performance]] of a [[task]] or [[duty]]; the [[action]] of [[cop out|copping out]].
#: {{ux|en|His disappearance on the day of the audition was just a '''cop-out'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} An [[excuse]] made in order to avoid performing a task or duty; a [[reason]] offered when someone cops out.
#: {{ux|en|It was a '''cop-out''' to say he couldn't sign the petition because he sprained his wrist.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[person]] who cops out.
#: {{ux|en|He's always a '''cop-out''' when there's hard work to be done.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=12 Aug 89|volume=17|number=5|journal=Gay Community Journal|page=8|author=Kate Rushin|title=Is Better Than Hollywood Good Enough?|text=Even when they are talking one-on-one, we aren't allowed to see behind the posturing and emblematic language. The major exception to this is Da Mayor {{...}} who is both scorned and respected, seen as both a '''cop-out''' and a hero.}}

